      "refersTo": "station-ring",
      "description": "A service stop: white ring with ink stroke, status dot inside, name and description; sign-in adds the outlined sign-in* tag. On the map the hostname fades in on hover/focus.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-station\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-rail\"></span><span class=\"ds-ring\"><span class=\"ds-dot\"></span></span><span class=\"ds-text\"><span class=\"ds-st\">Papra</span><span class=\"ds-desc\">Documents</span><span class=\"ds-tag\" aria-hidden=\"true\">sign-in<span class=\"ds-req\">*</span></span><span class=\"ds-host\">papra.lichnovsky.eu</span></span></a>",
      "css": ".ds-station{position:relative;display:flex;align-items:center;min-height:3.75rem;padding:.55rem 0 .55rem 76px;color:var(--ink,#0b1b4d);text-decoration:none;font-family:var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif)} .ds-rail{position:absolute;left:20px;top:0;bottom:0;width:8px;background:var(--apps,#9b0056)} .ds-ring{position:absolute;left:12px;top:50%;margin-top:-12px;display:grid;place-items:center;width:24px;height:24px;border:4px solid var(--ink,#0b1b4d);border-radius:50%;background:var(--ground,#fff)} .ds-dot{width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--up,#10a14d);transition:background-color .4s,opacity .4s} .ds-text{display:grid;gap:.05rem} .ds-st{font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3} .ds-desc{color:var(--ink-soft,#3d4a73);font-size:.9375rem;line-height:1.35} .ds-tag{justify-self:start;margin-top:.3rem;padding:.1rem .55rem 0;border:1.5px solid var(--ink-faint,#69739a);border-radius:999px;color:var(--ink-soft,#3d4a73);font:600 .75rem/1.4 var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif)} .ds-req{color:var(--tunnel-text,#b35600);font-weight:800} .ds-host{color:var(--ink-faint,#69739a);font:.90625rem/1.4 var(--mono,'Overpass Mono',monospace);opacity:0;transition:opacity .25s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)} .ds-station:hover .ds-host,.ds-station:focus-visible .ds-host{opacity:1} .ds-station:hover .ds-st,.ds-station:focus-visible .ds-st{text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:3px} .ds-station:focus-visible{outline:none} .ds-station:focus-visible .ds-ring{box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--ground,#fff),0 0 0 5px var(--ink,#0b1b4d)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Private Station",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "station-ring",
      "description": "Home-and-Tailscale-only stop: marked by the Victoria Blue ring alone; the access words live in the accessible name.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-pstation\" href=\"#\" aria-label=\"Jellyfin, Movies &amp; Shows, home and Tailscale only\"><span class=\"ds-pring\"><span class=\"ds-pdot\"></span></span><span class=\"ds-ptext\"><span class=\"ds-pst\">Jellyfin</span><span class=\"ds-pdesc\">Movies &amp; Shows</span></span></a>",
      "css": ".ds-pstation{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;color:var(--ink,#0b1b4d);text-decoration:none;font-family:var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif)} .ds-pring{display:grid;place-items:center;width:24px;height:24px;border:4px solid var(--tailscale,#0098d4);border-radius:50%;background:var(--ground,#fff)} .ds-pdot{width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--up,#10a14d)} .ds-ptext{display:grid} .ds-pst{font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:700} .ds-pdesc{color:var(--ink-soft,#3d4a73);font-size:.9375rem;line-height:1.35} .ds-pstation:hover .ds-pst,.ds-pstation:focus-visible .ds-pst{text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Planned Station",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "station-ring",
      "description": "Not deployed yet: dashed ink-faint ring, no dot, not linked.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-plan\"><span class=\"ds-plring\"></span><span class=\"ds-pltext\"><span class=\"ds-plst\">Immich</span><span class=\"ds-pldesc\">Photos</span><span class=\"ds-placc\">opening soon</span></span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-plan{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;font-family:var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif)} .ds-plring{width:24px;height:24px;border:4px dashed var(--ink-faint,#69739a);border-radius:50%;background:var(--ground,#fff)} .ds-pltext{display:grid} .ds-plst{color:var(--ink-faint,#69739a);font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:700} .ds-placc{color:var(--ink-faint,#69739a);font-size:.84375rem;font-weight:600} .ds-pldesc{color:var(--ink-soft,#3d4a73);font-size:.9375rem;line-height:1.35}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Line Bullet (Apps)",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "line-bullet-apps",
      "description": "The line's name on its colour.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-bullet-apps\">Apps</span>",
      "css": ".ds-bullet-apps{display:inline-block;padding:.1rem .55rem 0;border-radius:4px;background:var(--apps,#9b0056);color:#fff;font:700 .8125rem var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif);letter-spacing:.02em}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Line Bullet (Admin)",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "line-bullet-admin",
      "description": "Admin bullet uses Slate Grey so white text holds contrast.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-bullet-admin\">Admin</span>",
      "css": ".ds-bullet-admin{display:inline-block;padding:.1rem .55rem 0;border-radius:4px;background:var(--admin-text,#5f6972);color:#fff;font:700 .8125rem var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif);letter-spacing:.02em}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sign-in Tag",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "sign-in-tag",
      "description": "Outlined pill marking a sign-in station; the asterisk reads as \"required\".",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-tag\">sign-in<span class=\"ds-req\">*</span></span>",
      "css": ".ds-tag{display:inline-block;padding:.1rem .55rem 0;border:1.5px solid var(--ink-faint,#69739a);border-radius:999px;color:var(--ink-soft,#3d4a73);font:600 .75rem/1.4 var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif)} .ds-req{color:var(--tunnel-text,#b35600);font-weight:800}"
    },
    {
      "name": "You Are Here",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "you-are-here",
      "description": "Ink pill on the station for the page being read (lichnovsky.eu, first on the Apps line).",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-here\">You are here</span>",
      "css": ".ds-here{display:inline-block;padding:.1rem .55rem 0;border-radius:999px;background:var(--ink,#0b1b4d);color:var(--ground,#fff);font:700 .75rem/1.4 var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif);letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Status Line",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Overall status dot, summary link and checked time.",
      "html": "<p class=\"ds-status\"><span class=\"ds-sdot\"></span><span><a class=\"ds-sum\" href=\"#\">All services running</a><span class=\"ds-chk\">checked 14:02</span></span></p>",
      "css": ".ds-status{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:.6rem;margin:0;color:var(--ink-soft,#3d4a73);font:.9375rem var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif)} .ds-sdot{flex:none;width:.625rem;height:.625rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--up,#10a14d);transition:background-color .4s,opacity .4s} .ds-sum{color:var(--ink,#0b1b4d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none} .ds-sum:hover{text-decoration:underline} .ds-sum:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ink,#0b1b4d);outline-offset:3px;border-radius:2px} .ds-chk{margin-left:.6rem;color:var(--ink-faint,#69739a)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Key",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Line swatches as flat bars, station states as miniature rings.",
      "html": "<ul class=\"ds-key\"><li><i class=\"ds-sw\" style=\"background:var(--tunnel,#ee7c0e)\"></i>Internet</li><li><i class=\"ds-sw\" style=\"background:var(--tailscale,#0098d4)\"></i>Anywhere</li><li><b class=\"ds-mini ds-up\"></b>running</li><li><b class=\"ds-mini ds-down\"></b>down</li><li><b class=\"ds-mini ds-plan-mini\"></b>opening soon</li><li><b class=\"ds-mini ds-priv\"></b>home &amp; Tailscale only</li><li><em class=\"ds-ktag\">sign-in<span class=\"ds-kreq\">*</span></em><span class=\"ds-gloss\">sign-in required through Cloudflare Access</span></li></ul>",
      "css": ".ds-key{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem 1.6rem;margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;color:var(--ink,#0b1b4d);font:600 .875rem var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif)} .ds-key li{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem} .ds-sw{width:1.75rem;height:.4375rem} .ds-mini{display:grid;place-items:center;width:1.125rem;height:1.125rem;border:3px solid var(--ink,#0b1b4d);border-radius:50%} .ds-mini::after{content:'';width:.375rem;height:.375rem;border-radius:50%} .ds-up::after{background:var(--up,#10a14d)} .ds-down::after{background:var(--down,#dc241f)} .ds-plan-mini{border-style:dashed;border-color:var(--ink-faint,#69739a)} .ds-priv{border-color:var(--tailscale,#0098d4)} .ds-priv::after{background:var(--up,#10a14d)} .ds-ktag{padding:.05rem .5rem 0;border:1.5px solid var(--ink-faint,#69739a);border-radius:999px;color:var(--ink-soft,#3d4a73);font-size:.8125rem;font-style:normal;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap} .ds-kreq{color:var(--tunnel-text,#b35600);font-weight:800} .ds-gloss{color:var(--ink-soft,#3d4a73);font-weight:400}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Link",
      "kind": "nav",
      "description": "Inline and secondary links.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-link\" href=\"#\">Back to the map</a> <a class=\"ds-gh\" href=\"#\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"8\" r=\"8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/></svg>github.com/jersyj/lichnovsky</a>",
      "css": ".ds-link{color:var(--ink,#0b1b4d);font:700 1rem var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif);text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:.25em} .ds-link:focus-visible,.ds-gh:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ink,#0b1b4d);outline-offset:3px;border-radius:2px} .ds-gh{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-left:1.5rem;color:var(--ink-soft,#3d4a73);font:.9375rem var(--sans,'Overpass Variable',sans-serif);text-decoration:none} .ds-gh:hover{color:var(--ink,#0b1b4d);text-decoration:underline}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Night Service Map",
    "overview": "The whole site is a Beck-style transit diagram of the homelab. Three ways in (Internet through the Cloudflare Tunnel, Home LAN, Anywhere over Tailscale) run left to right into the rpi-01 interchange. The Apps and Admin lines leave it side by side, then split at 45 degrees to a station for every service; this page itself (lichnovsky.eu) is the first station on the Apps line. Nothing is a card, a tile, or a dashboard panel: every service is a white ring on a coloured line, and its live state is the dot inside that ring.\n\nThe material is enamel signage: a white ground, station names in corporate navy, flat line colours with no gradients or shading, and one typeface family doing all the work. Density is low and the page is quiet on purpose; the diagram carries the \"wow\" through geometry and a single drawing-in animation, not ornament. Dark mode is the night service: the same lines, slightly brightened, on a navy ground.\n\nOn phones the map becomes the in-carriage line strip: the ways in stack and join at the Pi, then the Apps and Admin rails run down the left edge with one stop per service. It is the same system at a different scale, not a different layout language.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Transit-diagram geometry: horizontal runs and 45-degree bends only, round line joins.",
      "Flat line colours from the London palette; status colours reserved for status.",
      "White ring stations with an ink stroke; the status dot sits inside the ring.",
      "Stations say name and description; access is a mark (an outlined \"sign-in*\" tag for sign-in, a Victoria Blue ring for home-only), and hostnames appear only when a map station is pointed at.",
      "Overpass for everything, Overpass Mono only for hostnames.",
      "Light and night variants follow the system colour scheme.",
      "One drawing-in sequence on load and one route-highlight interaction; reduced motion shows the finished map."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Green Belongs To Status Rule",
        "body": "Green, red and amber mean up, down and pending, nothing else. No line, link, accent or decoration may use them.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Text-Tone Pair Rule",
        "body": "When a line colour must be read as text or carry white text (Overground Orange, Victoria Blue, Jubilee Grey), use its `-text` partner token, never the line colour itself.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Is For Machines Rule",
        "body": "Overpass Mono appears only on hostnames. Labels, notes, status text and headings stay in Overpass.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The 12px Floor Rule",
        "body": "No map text renders below 12px at any viewport; between 1000px and 1120px the small map labels lift to 16px map units and the sign-in tag and \"You are here\" pill scale 1.15 to hold the floor.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Enamel Rule",
        "body": "Every surface is flat printed colour. Dimming (opacity 0.16) is the only way something recedes.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** draw every new route with horizontal runs and 45-degree bends only, 12-unit lines with round joins.",
      "**Do** add a service as a new station on its line from `services.ts`; never hand-place markup.",
      "**Do** put status in the dot inside the ring, and expose it as text too (title, accessible name, summary line).",
      "**Do** use the `-text` partner token whenever a line colour is read as text or carries white text.",
      "**Do** mark access with the system's own devices (the outlined \"sign-in*\" tag with its asterisk in tunnel-text, the Victoria Blue ring for home-only), explain both in the key, and put the words in the accessible name.",
      "**Do** show \"not open yet\" with dashes: dashed line sections and dashed ink-faint rings.",
      "**Do** keep every animation inside `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference` and show the finished state otherwise."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use green, red or amber for anything except status.",
      "**Don't** add cards, tiles, icon grids, shadows or gradients; the world is flat enamel signage.",
      "**Don't** use Overpass Mono for anything but hostnames.",
      "**Don't** let map text fall below 12px rendered.",
      "**Don't** bend a line at any angle other than 45 degrees."
    ]
  }
}
